5.  NUMBER THEORY PROBLEMS AND SOLUTIONS
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[Adam Number]
    Definition:
        12 → reverse → 21
        12² = 144
        21² = 441 → reverse → 144 == 12²  → Adam number

    Steps:
        1. Compute square of input (sq).
        2. Reverse the input (rev).
        3. Compute square of rev (sq_rev).
        4. Reverse sq_rev (rev_sq_rev).
        5. If sq == rev_sq_rev → Adam number.

    Solution:
        #include <stdio.h>
        int reverse(int n) {
            int r = 0;
            while (n) {
                r = r * 10 + n % 10;
                n /= 10;
            }
            return r;
        }
        int main() {
            int num;
            scanf("%d", &num);
            int sq = num * num;
            int rev = reverse(num);
            int sq_rev = rev * rev;
            if (sq == reverse(sq_rev))
                printf("Adam number\n");
            else
                printf("Not Adam number\n");
            return 0;
        }

