[Happy Number]
    Example: 82
    8² + 2² = 68 → 6²+8² = 100 → 1²+0²+0² = 1 → Happy

    Steps:
        1. While n != 1 and not repeating (loop detection can be added),
           replace n by sum of squares of its digits.
        2. If n becomes 1 → Happy number.

    Solution (simple, but may loop infinitely for non‑happy; we can limit iterations):
        #include <stdio.h>
        int sum_sq(int n) {
            int s = 0, d;
            while (n) {
                d = n % 10;
                s += d * d;
                n /= 10;
            }
            return s;
        }
        int main() {
            int n, slow, fast;
            scanf("%d", &n);
            slow = fast = n;
            do {
                slow = sum_sq(slow);
                fast = sum_sq(sum_sq(fast));
            } while (slow != fast);
            if (slow == 1)
                printf("Happy number\n");
            else
                printf("Not Happy number\n");
            return 0;
        }

    (The Floyd’s cycle detection is used here to avoid infinite loops.)

