[Abundant Number]
    Sum of proper divisors > number.
    Example: 20 → 1+2+4+5+10 = 22 > 20.

    Steps: Same as perfect, check sum > n.

    Solution:
        #include <stdio.h>
        #include <math.h>
        int main() {
            int n, sum = 1;
            scanf("%d", &n);
            for (int i = 2; i <= sqrt(n); i++) {
                if (n % i == 0) {
                    sum += i;
                    if (i != n/i) sum += n/i;
                }
            }
            if (sum > n) printf("Abundant number\n");
            else printf("Not Abundant number\n");
            return 0;
        }

