[Mersenne Number]
    A number that is one less than a power of two: 2ⁿ – 1.
    Binary representation is all 1's. Example: 3, 7, 15, 31, 63, 127, …

    Steps:
        1. Check if n+1 is a power of two: (n+1) & n == 0.
        2. If true and n>1 → Mersenne.

    Solution:
        #include <stdio.h>
        int main() {
            int n;
            scanf("%d", &n);
            if (n > 1 && ((n+1) & n) == 0)
                printf("Mersenne number\n");
            else
                printf("Not Mersenne number\n");
            return 0;
        }

