[Harshad Number (Niven Number)]
    A number divisible by the sum of its digits.
    Example: 12 → sum=3, 12%3==0.

    Solution:
        #include <stdio.h>
        int main() {
            int n, sum = 0, temp;
            scanf("%d", &n);
            temp = n;
            while (temp) {
                sum += temp % 10;
                temp /= 10;
            }
            if (n % sum == 0)
                printf("Harshad number\n");
            else
                printf("Not Harshad number\n");
            return 0;
        }

