[Fibonacci Number]
    A number in the Fibonacci sequence: 0,1,1,2,3,5,8,13,...
    Check: n is Fibonacci iff (5*n² + 4) or (5*n² - 4) is a perfect square.

    Solution:
        #include <stdio.h>
        #include <math.h>
        int isPerfectSquare(int x) {
            int s = sqrt(x);
            return (s*s == x);
        }
        int main() {
            int n;
            scanf("%d", &n);
            if (isPerfectSquare(5*n*n + 4) || isPerfectSquare(5*n*n - 4))
                printf("Fibonacci number\n");
            else
                printf("Not Fibonacci number\n");
            return 0;
        }

