[Amicable Pairs]
    Two numbers are amicable if sum of proper divisors of each equals the other.
    Example: 220 and 284.
    Check: sum_div(220)=284, sum_div(284)=220.

    We'll just check if a given pair (a,b) is amicable.

    Solution:
        #include <stdio.h>
        int sum_div(int n) {
            int sum = 1;
            for (int i = 2; i * i <= n; i++) {
                if (n % i == 0) {
                    sum += i;
                    if (i != n/i) sum += n/i;
                }
            }
            return sum;
        }
        int main() {
            int a, b;
            scanf("%d %d", &a, &b);
            if (sum_div(a) == b && sum_div(b) == a)
                printf("Amicable pair\n");
            else
                printf("Not Amicable pair\n");
            return 0;
        }

