[Strobogrammatic Number]
    A number that reads the same when rotated 180 degrees.
    Valid digits: 0,1,8, (6 and 9 become each other).
    Example: 69 → rotated 180 becomes 69 (same) → strobogrammatic.
    For numeric checking: reverse with mapping: 0→0, 1→1, 6→9, 8→8, 9→6; if the mapped reversed equals original, it's strobogrammatic.

    Solution:
        #include <stdio.h>
        int main() {
            int n, temp, rot = 0, valid = 1;
            scanf("%d", &n);
            temp = n;
            while (temp) {
                int d = temp % 10;
                if (d == 0 || d == 1 || d == 8) rot = rot * 10 + d;
                else if (d == 6) rot = rot * 10 + 9;
                else if (d == 9) rot = rot * 10 + 6;
                else { valid = 0; break; }
                temp /= 10;
            }
            if (valid && rot == n)
                printf("Strobogrammatic number\n");
            else
                printf("Not Strobogrammatic number\n");
            return 0;
        }

